WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.502
-I'm so happy to see you
every time.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.169
How's everything going upstairs
on "Saturday Night Live?"

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:05.338
-It's crazy.
-It's nuts, right?

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.706
-It's a lot of moving around.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.275
It's a lot of duties
and responsibilities.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.777
But it's amazing.
-Did you ever think

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.612
that you would ever host
and musical guest?

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.382
-It honestly has been a dream
for me since I was a little kid.

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:18.851
My older cousin Chris

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:23.423
used to have all this
MC Hammer memorabilia.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.891
-Sure.
-I guess it wasn't memorabilia,

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.959
'cause it was current.
-At the time.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:30.029
-Yeah. At the time, it was --
Yeah, but now it's memorabilia.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.730
-It was passed down to me,
and it became memorabilia,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.367
and he had all this stuff, and
one of them was a VHS recording

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.870
of MC Hammer hosting
and musical guest at "SNL."

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.805
So I just always
wanted to do that.

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.240
-Since Hammer.
-Since Hammer.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.909
-Hammer time, man, yeah.
-Got out the hammer, yo.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.043
-Absolutely.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.178
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.281
Last time you were on our show,

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.350
we announced the name
of the album,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.651
the release date.
-Yes.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.586
-And it was a big deal.
-We did a lot that day.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.421
-We did a lot that day.
We got a lot accomplished.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.089
And since then,
it's been streamed

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:01.160
over 100 million times
on Spotify.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.296
-Thanks to you guys.
Thanks to you.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:06.298
-I mean, come on. "Big Day."

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:08.902
"The Big Day"
is the name of the record,

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.172
but honestly, this is kind of
inspired by your actual big day.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:13.606
-Yeah.
-You got married.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.041
And you had a beautiful wedding.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.910
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.544
-Oh, hey.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.580
That's gorgeous.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.882
-That's a nice ring.
Here's a picture of --

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.150
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.984
Here's a picture
of your wedding party.

00:01:25.984 --> 00:01:27.753
-I saw you posted this --

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.922
Everyone's wearing -- Yeah,
everyone's wearing a nice tuxedo

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.257
except for Kanye.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.759
That's fine.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.195
He's always getting
into trouble, man. Come on.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.530
No, you just can't tell Kanye
what to do.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.898
-He does his --
He does his thing.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.200
-No, he does his thing.
How is he as a wedding guest?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.235
Is he a fun wedding guest?
-Yeah, he's awesome.

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:47.406
What I remember is he tried
to join the wedding band.

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:49.542
Like, they were playing music.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.743
-Really?

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.879
-But he didn't have his setup,
his beat machine,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.947
so he just kind of
stood next to them.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.216
We're like, "What --"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.851
-He's ready to go.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.586
If someone had a beat machine,
he would have been there.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.154
-He would've been there.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:03.956
-You delayed your tour...
-Yeah.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.524
-...for a good reason.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.126
-And I want to show everyone
the good reason.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.160
-Yeah.
-You just had your --

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.361
Is this your second daughter?

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:10.830
-Yes, that's
my youngest daughter.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.899
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.367
-Aww.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.936
-That's my baby.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.970
Yeah.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.171
-How beautiful is that?

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:20.440
-Yeah, she --

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.474
I'm on --

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.042
-Two little girls.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.677
-Yeah, two beautiful girls.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.246
Yeah, I'm on paternity leave
right now.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.281
-Yeah, just doing your -- Yeah.

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:30.750
-Taking care of business
at home.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.785
-Say goodbye to sleep, yeah.
Sleep is gone.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.053
How old is the oldest?

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:37.189
-She's 4. Kensli's 4,
and Marli is 2 months now.

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.557
It's crazy, actually.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.660
Kensli's first time
being on a flight

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.329
was to come to my first
"SNL" performance,

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.665
and now my youngest
daughter Marli

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.434
just got off of her first flight
to come see me at "SNL."

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.636
-That's her first flight.
That's good luck for you.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:51.737
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.373
-That's great.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.442
[ Applause ]

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.512
Not only do I like your music,
but I like you as a person, too.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.013
You're great to talk to.
-Thank you.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:03.916
-But as a philanthropist,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:07.853
you give so much back
to your hometown of Chicago.

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:11.624
You've given $1 million
to Chicago public schools.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.527
You've given...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.328
...$1 million

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:19.899
to mental health services
in Chicago, which is --

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.235
I love that you do that.
I really do.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:24.504
I love that you do that.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.973
Tell me about --
What is OpenMike?

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.209
-Oh, OpenMike.
Oh, that's a good one, yeah.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:33.379
So, in Chicago,
my nonprofit SocialWorks

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.348
has an open mic program
that we do once a month,

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:39.785
and basically, it's kind of
the antithesis of a talent show.

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.188
We just have kids
that are young creators,

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:46.025
whether they're writers
or, you know, rappers, poets,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:49.295
dancers, comedians, actors,

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.363
like, just young kids
that are in high school come up,

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:53.199
and they get
three minutes onstage

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.001
to do and say
whatever they want to do.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.938
And hopefully, you know,
the next "SNL" guest or host

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.472
is coming out of the program.

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:03.209
-Yeah, absolutely.
I hope so. Hope that's true.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.511
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.315
I think you're the only album --

00:04:10.315 --> 00:04:14.620
You're the only artist out there
that has a duet with --

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.555
I'm just going to name some
names right here.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.191
I mean, En Vogue.

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.758
You have --

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:22.061
Yeah, sure.
Megan Thee Stallion --

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:25.397
You have Megan Thee Stallion and
Randy Newman on the same album.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:26.799
-Randy Newman's on there.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.634
-I mean, who does that?

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.302
I mean, it's great. Gucci Mane.

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:31.571
I mean, these are --

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.606
I just love
that you see Nicki Minaj

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.208
and then Randy Newman just
keeps popping back up again.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.010
How did you get involved
with Randy Newman?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.180
-I mean, I've always wanted
to work with Randy Newman.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.350
The first movie my parents
took me to the theaters to see

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:48.454
was "Toy Story," so I just like,
from a young age, was familiar.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.323
And then I got more familiar
as I got older, and --

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:52.525
-You love him.
-Yeah, he's just --

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.259
He's an amazing artist.
Great to work with.

00:04:54.259 --> 00:04:56.395
Everybody on the album,
for the most part, you know,

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:57.897
came to Chicago to work with me

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:01.067
and just, like, put
a great energy into it.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.235
I think it's such a diverse cast

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:06.238
because so many, you know,
different sounds

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.473
that you play
on your wedding day.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.675
So they all kind of tap in
in different places.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:11.911
-It's a great record,
and you're a great dude.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.012
-Thank you, thank you.
-Always good to see you.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.379
Chance the Rapper, everybody.

00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:16.549
"The Big Day" is available now.

